        "original_id": "2336eb5c-9b43-5127-8292-ff01a0b86712",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Daniel Craig, Stephen Tompkinson, Terence Gross, Toni Collette\n- Works: Hotel Splendide, Casino Royale, Brassed Off, Inspector Alan Banks, DCI Banks, James Bond\n- Topics: film and television casting, adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- In 1996, Stephen Tompkinson starred in the film \"Brassed Off.\"\n- In 2000, \"Hotel Splendide\" was released as a British independent dark comedy film written and directed by Terence Gross and starring Toni Collette and Daniel Craig.\n- In 2000, Stephen Tompkinson also starred in the film \"Hotel Splendide.\"\n- Since 2010, several \"Inspector Alan Banks\" novels have been adapted for television as the series \"DCI Banks\" with Stephen Tompkinson in the lead role.\n- In October 2005, Daniel Craig was cast as the British secret agent James Bond.\n- In November 2006, Daniel Craig's first James Bond film, \"Casino Royale,\" was released internationally.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
